b.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- 4.6.2 (but this is the same for all 4.x)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Linux Mint 22.2 (Zara) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated Intel(R) Arc(tm) A770 Graphics (DG2) - AMD Ryzen 9 8945HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 28.21 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen transcoding a BasisU texture we check which VRAM compressed formats are supported. Then we select the destination format based on what is supported in this Priority order BPTC -> ASTC -> S3TC -> ETC2 -> RAW\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/613213c0150b830d29ecaa3fa3525e4a5e0abdc8/modules/basis_universal/image_compress_basisu.cpp#L377-L393\n\nThis logic doesn't make sense since any platform that supports S3TC also supports BPTC. Which means it will effectively always select BPTC which has 2X the storage requirement of S3TC. Also, any platform that supports both ASTC and BPTC should use ASTC since ASTC is a higher quality format and is faster to transcode to. \n\nUltimately, while BPTC is a higher quality format, it should be used only when needed because it requires 2X as much VRAM as S3TC. \n\n_Note: Looking at the surrounding code, I see other questionable format choices, like preferring DXT1 over DXT4 for single channel data. BC4 has the same compression ratio as DXT1 except it looks almost indistinguishable from uncompressed (whereas DXT1 looks horrible)_\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Select any texture (icon.png will be fine)\n2. Select import settings\n3. Select Basis Universal\n4. Double click on texture in filesystem and observe that it is using BPTC/ASTC\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120000/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120000/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}